<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2010/07/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>VL.GIS.Skia</id>
    <!--
      Versioned alongside VL.GIS rather than independently. They are released together and
      VL.GIS.Skia is meaningless without a matching VL.GIS, so two moving numbers would only
      create combinations nobody has tested.
    -->
    <version>0.2.0-alpha</version>
    <title>VL.GIS.Skia — 2D map rendering helpers for VL.GIS</title>
    <authors>VL.GIS Contributors</authors>
    <owners>VL.GIS Contributors</owners>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <readme>docs\README.md</readme>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/rednotfound/vvvv-gis</projectUrl>
    <description>
      EARLY - please be careful about using this in a real project yet.

      Puts a map on screen in vvvv gamma, by supplying the arithmetic VL.Skia needs rather
      than drawing anything itself. Styling stays in the patch.

      - GIS.Skia.Viewport: a centre, a zoom and a pixel size; screen positions, view bounds,
        panning, and zooming around a fixed pixel
      - GIS.Skia.Tiles: which tiles a view needs, and the SKRect each one belongs in
      - GIS.Skia.Paths: NetTopologySuite geometry to SKPath, in screen space

      Wire the output into VL.Skia's ImageLayer and DrawPath.

      Requires VL.GIS and vvvv gamma 7.2 or newer (.NET 8).
    </description>
    <summary>Map viewport, tile placement and geometry-to-SKPath nodes for VL.GIS.</summary>
    <releaseNotes>
      0.2.0-alpha - First release. Sixteen nodes covering viewport maths, tile layout and
      geometry to SKPath, verified by 39 tests.

      An OSM tile does reach the screen: help\HowTo Show a map.vl draws one in vvvv 7.4.
      One tile, not many - a multi-tile patch needs a ForEach region and has not been built.
      An earlier claim of "20 seamless tiles" came from an offscreen SKCanvas probe that
      bypassed VL's coordinate space entirely, so it is not evidence about vvvv and has been
      withdrawn.

      Note ToRendererSpace, which converts view pixels into the units the renderer actually
      draws in. It is not optional: VL.Skia's default space spans roughly 2.8 by 2 units, so
      a pixel coordinate handed straight to a layer node lands far off screen with nothing
      drawn and no error.

      Draws nothing itself. VL.Skia already has DrawImage and DrawPath, and what a map looks
      like belongs to whoever is patching it.
    </releaseNotes>
    <copyright>Copyright 2026 VL.GIS Contributors</copyright>
    <!-- The "VL" tag is what makes the pack discoverable at https://vvvv.org/packs -->
    <tags>VL vvvv gamma gis geospatial map tiles skia rendering</tags>
    <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/rednotfound/vvvv-gis" />

    <!--
      SkiaSharp is deliberately absent, for the same reason VL.Core and VL.CoreLib are:
      it ships inside vvvv, which substitutes its own copy for anything declared here.
      VL.Skia is likewise part of vvvv and is declared in VL.GIS.Skia.vl instead.
    -->
    <dependencies>
      <group targetFramework="net8.0">
        <dependency id="VL.GIS"                      version="0.2.0-alpha" />
        <dependency id="NetTopologySuite"            version="2.6.0" />
        <dependency id="BruTile"                     version="6.0.0" />
      </group>
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <files>
    <!-- Entry point. Must sit at the package root, no subfolder. -->
    <file src="VL.GIS.Skia.vl" target="" />

    <file src="src\VL.GIS.Skia\bin\Release\net8.0\VL.GIS.Skia.dll" target="lib\net8.0\" />
    <file src="src\VL.GIS.Skia\bin\Release\net8.0\VL.GIS.Skia.xml" target="lib\net8.0\" />

    <!--
      This package's own examples only. help\ is split by package name so that a patch needing
      VL.GIS.Skia ships here rather than with VL.GIS, where it would open with a missing
      dependency. target stays help\ because that is where vvvv looks.
    -->
    <file src="help\VL.GIS.Skia\**\*.vl" target="help\" />

    <file src="README.md"              target="docs\" />
    <file src="THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md" target="docs\" />
  </files>
</package>
